<title>SWEDEN: Scania 9 mo profit falls 39 percent.</title>
<headline>Scania 9 mo profit falls 39 percent.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck company Scania results for nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  2,142 vs   3,512</p>
<p> Sales					24,566 vs  25,442</p>
<p> Operating profit			  2,429 vs   3,888</p>
<p> EPS (SKR)				    7.65 vs   11.57</p>
<p> Operating costs			  21,381 vs 20,860</p>
<p> Profit pre deprec			 3,185 vs  4,582</p>
<p> Depreciation				  977 vs    915</p>
<p> Associate interests			 221 vs    221</p>
<p> Profit after deprec		     2,429 vs  3,888</p>
<p> Financial items			     287 vs    376</p>
<p> Tax					     616 vs  1,198</p>
<p> Minorities			     CREDIT 4 vs	1 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,530 vs  2,313</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is Scania. Scania said invoiced trucks/buses for the nine months fell to 31,872 against 32,299 a year.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 11 analysts found an average forecast for profit after financial items of 2.65 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
